  "Question": "Which of the following sets of whole numbers has the largest average?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "multiples of \\(2\\) between \\(1\\) and \\(101\\)",
    "B": "multiples of \\(3\\) between \\(1\\) and \\(101\\)",
    "C": "multiples of \\(4\\) between \\(1\\) and \\(101\\)",
    "D": "multiples of \\(5\\) between \\(1\\) and\n\\(101\\)",
    "E": "multiples of \\(6\\) between \\(1\\) and \\(101\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each set consists of equally spaced numbers. Pair the smallest with the largest, the next smallest with the next largest, and continue inward. Every pair has the same sum, so the average of the whole set is the average of its first and last numbers. If one middle number remains, it equals that same average.\n\nThe first and last multiples in each set give\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{A: }&\\frac{2+100}{2}=51,\\\\\n\\text{B: }&\\frac{3+99}{2}=51,\\\\\n\\text{C: }&\\frac{4+100}{2}=52,\\\\\n\\text{D: }&\\frac{5+100}{2}=52.5,\\\\\n\\text{E: }&\\frac{6+96}{2}=51.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe largest average is \\(52.5\\), obtained by the multiples of \\(5\\), choice D.",
